It looks like your surprise deadly attack made you dreadful opponents in the eyes of the natives, almost equal to gods. Some savages dropped their spears and ran into the forest yelling in fear. Some fell on their knees shaking, covering their heads with their hands. When you found yourselves on the clearing where the natives were dancing, some sudden movement from the right drew your attention. You quickly turn and see a cage with Snoopy in it. He barks and jumps at the cage bars, showing his joy, as if he is not captured on the alien island.

But you don't look at Snoopy. You look at one of the savages, slain by Conan's shot. This is a young bloke, a bit older than you. A grimace of pain, astonishment, and fear is solidified on his once handsome face. A large pool of blood shows black beneath him. It seems the bullet pierced his heart, and death was instantaneous.

"These were enemies!" you reiterate to yourself. "They deserved it! These were enemies!"